{"title":"2026 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 19","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_19\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 19</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Set_the_Distance_and_Speed!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Set the Distance and Speed!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Quick)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Quick)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_7_-_Cheese_🧀\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 7 - Cheese 🧀</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_DDM\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by DDM</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Thinking_Feet\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Thinking Feet</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_in_Chinese_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution in Chinese by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_19\">Problem 19</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 19\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Miguel is walking with his dog, Luna. When they reach the entrance to a park, Miguel throws a ball straight ahead and continues to walk at a steady pace. Luna sprints toward the ball, which stops by a tree. As soon as the dog reaches the ball, she brings it back to Miguel. Luna runs 5 times faster than Miguel walks. What fraction of the distance between the entrance and the tree does Miguel cover by the time Luna brings him the ball?\n</p><p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Amc_8_2026_q19.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/5/5b/Amc_8_2026_q19.png/650px-Amc_8_2026_q19.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"650\" height=\"130\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/5/5b/Amc_8_2026_q19.png 1.5x\" /></a></span>\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/b/c6b8b8ec505259eff44ae17174537234f55ee836.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } \\frac{1}{6}\\qquad\\textbf{(B) } \\frac{1}{5}\\qquad\\textbf{(C) } \\frac{1}{4}\\qquad\\textbf{(D) } \\frac{1}{3}\\qquad\\textbf{(E) } \\frac{2}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"375\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let Miguel's speed equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />. That makes Luna's speed <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/5/0a5ce1993a19289a83ada79834e8bc758b1b8675.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5s$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />. Let the distance between the park entrance and the tree be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. The total distance covered by Miguel and Luna is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/1/5b18a6d2a2364c593dcfa9d33a586437687fa149.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s + 5s = 6s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"92\" height=\"15\" />, which is also equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/8/808d70ce29110acbfa47228747db2e682cf103ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2d$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" />. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/9/d89283f43d7b85f5993acad0b90b7ad0a78c7243.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6s = 2d \\Rightarrow s = \\boxed{ \\textbf{(D) } \\frac{1}{3}}d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"193\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~OlympiadMaster\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The distance between the park entrance and the tree is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. Then, the rate that Miguel walks is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/f/a9f23bf124b6b2b2a993eb313c72e678664ac74a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, and Luna runs at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/c/4ec4e27d0fae082b6525d7585ed44fadfaf3fbd1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5v$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. As Luna runs the distance <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and back, she runs a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/b/18bcad235e4dd1cbd76dc64b406ce29ab06135c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x - m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"60\" height=\"15\" /> (where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is the amount that Miguel walks). Then, because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/5/8650a100ae4f00e8aaed2319f3f411bc86a9c55c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d/s = t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"60\" height=\"20\" /> (where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is distance, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> is time, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> is speed), It takes Luna <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/d/aad090c8531ec3272d1012eed01f80346bb11984.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2x - m}{5v}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"63\" height=\"38\" /> time to reach back to Miguel. Also, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/c/dec51eda216482dc8bc7eabf0b33178793ddd0ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d = st$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />, and by that time, Miguel traveled <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/4/7c40c13b40752ed98310e7cd6ac7587b78aebcf8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = v\\left(\\frac{2x - m}{5v}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"142\" height=\"45\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/7/96793a9d73ad0cfada07e2c76df94397ef183e08.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5m = 2x - m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"109\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/b/6bb5123e0168938710d074786a2dcd0d08a5d79d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6m = 2x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"71\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/9/94982b34e6b5107a00ee7221698422aa935417cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3m = x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"62\" height=\"14\" />. The total distance from the park to the tree is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/0/7603b770794a22f4204b4d232283650519576807.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3m$\" width=\"24\" height=\"12\" />, and Miguel traversed <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />, giving us a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/2/ce299289fd00b98ef583bffe42bbf5d7700da3b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{3m} = \\boxed{\\frac{1}{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"79\" height=\"49\" /> the distance traveled.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Set_the_Distance_and_Speed.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Set_the_Distance_and_Speed!)\">Solution 3 (Set the Distance and Speed!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Set the Distance and Speed!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The distance doesn't seem to matter as if it did, then the problem would have told the distance, so lets say the distance is 30 units. Also the speed of Luna doesn't matter as the ratio of Luna's speed to Miguel's speed is 5:1, always the same. We can say that Luna goes 5 units a second, then that means that Miguel goes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/6/f16827c665914fb4e6202bc859799ef14e3e3b9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5}{5} =1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"48\" height=\"38\" /> units a second. Luna will reach the tree after <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/3/7035026e267534753ae9a3e59f0d32ee9e1f6e11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{30}{5} =6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"57\" height=\"38\" /> seconds. When Luna reaches the tree Miguel will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/d/e6d7e650ff8a60fd9555b2f0ad3bcc4a90d7fb25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 \\times 1 = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" /> units from the entrance of the park. We can set up the equations: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/9/2b9e21ddfef0c96085b80290dc156cc9f0867ca2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/8/bc86654434f9e43e2ed12717e9d4ca0645190583.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-5x+30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" />, where x represents seconds as Miguel is 6 units from the entrance is walking away at a rate of 1 unit a second and Luna is 30 units from the entrance and is walking towards the entrance at a rate of 5 units a second. We can now set both equations equal together to find out how far away from the entrance they meet. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/1/491bdc56c9de8b2df633e7805fdd5a917c3af578.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+6=-5x+30 \\implies 6x=24 \\implies x=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"346\" height=\"15\" />. This means that they meet 4 seconds after Luna reaches the tree, this means they meet after <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/b/5fb63be3aea0e2c2da7142ece73318974b0a6940.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4+6=10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"82\" height=\"14\" /> seconds as Luna takes 6 seconds to reach the tree. In <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> seconds Miguel travels <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/f/8efc58f934a68e629cf9dcf8b144c1c0fe0cba6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10 \\times 1=10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" /> units, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/c/82c141a7b91e461dfaa896bd5a491842358dc64e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{10}{30} = \\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"61\" height=\"38\" />, giving us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/6/8363ecc686113b1d0cce7b74ec234541e43302f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\frac{1}{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"24\" height=\"48\" />\n~ Shaarav14 for Carnage MS\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since Luna is 5 times faster than Miguel, Miguel gets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/2/d129a7b3c0bf9fbd0693afdd426a66d2a0a8c3ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" />  of the way to the tree by the time Luna reaches the ball. The ratio of Miguel´s speed to Luna´s is 1:5, and the distance between Miguel and the tree is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/d/4fd03d5b164ae8b40db27a6f8ddb20d9d43f95fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> the distance between the entrance and the tree. So Miguel walks another <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/f/18f7367c45dd5571abfc512373ff1d4bbf573882.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4}{5} \\times \\frac{1}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"50\" height=\"38\" /> of the way from the entrance to the tree by the time Luna comes back to him. Therefore, Miguel walks <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/0/33014d140c67af52839ac42d515aec3d3176b0aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{5} + \\frac{4}{30}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"59\" height=\"38\" /> =<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/6/8363ecc686113b1d0cce7b74ec234541e43302f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\frac{1}{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"24\" height=\"48\" /> of the way to the tree from the entrance.\n-Pillowwillowtree01\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Quick.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Quick)\">Solution 5 (Quick)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Quick)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since Luna runs 5 times faster than Miguel walks, by the time Luna reaches the tree, Miguel has walked <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/2/d129a7b3c0bf9fbd0693afdd426a66d2a0a8c3ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> of the distance from the entrance to the tree. This eliminates answer choices <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/5/ec5bdc2c0e59651ee5e6fa74ba318dc73d744feb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"24\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/2/5e226c2f5a445f0a9ab589c1337336ea7587b36e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(B)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>This is a multiple-choice problem with the remaining answers listed in increasing order, so we test the middle option, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/d/87d32bac8c5abe4d6b299d444f24a8055279b232.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(D)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"24\" height=\"17\" />, which corresponds to Miguel walking <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1965f8d70832ded66434c75a7bd52b75090af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> of the distance.\n</p><p>If Miguel walks a total distance of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1965f8d70832ded66434c75a7bd52b75090af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />, then the additional distance he walks while Luna is running back toward him is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/e/d2e0c53010341d7817bceff46a51498d9ed2608e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{1}{5}=\\frac{2}{15}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"97\" height=\"38\" />. Since Luna runs 5 times faster than Miguel walks, she covers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/8/d18e6e64c57175e1c0a61c686c85130b4a88940a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5\\cdot\\frac{2}{15}=\\frac{2}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"84\" height=\"38\" /> of the distance on her return.\n</p><p>Thus, Luna runs the entire distance to the tree and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/4/7547747b133453d3c209cff6cfbf129aa67a6947.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> of the distance back, while Miguel walks <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1965f8d70832ded66434c75a7bd52b75090af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> of the distance forward, so they meet at the same point. Therefore, the fraction of the distance Miguel covers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/6/8363ecc686113b1d0cce7b74ec234541e43302f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\frac{1}{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"24\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p><p>~jeremyq\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6\">Solution 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Because Luna is running five times as fast as Miguel, when the two meet, Luna will have run five times as far. We can call the distance from the place where Miguel threw the ball to the tree <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, and the distance that Miguel runs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. When the two meet they will have run a combined total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/f/04f2a4fd36328639598a2ab07d12d933f187bc4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"27\" height=\"14\" />. Miguel runs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and because she runs five times as fast, Luna runs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/7/cf73c86bd37c9b167d81d84f3c9b12c4b00799e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"26\" height=\"14\" />. There combined total is therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/1/3c15b95d401c6cd1efe71d1c28ebc937a5faaa9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y+5Y=6Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"110\" height=\"16\" />. So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/9/529aa7333b842b1f88371c488fc1fc9a8d3a00c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6Y=2x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"69\" height=\"14\" />. The value we are trying to find is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/a/93a32fa55c08ac66b211414f28160911896ac45d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{Y}{X}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"22\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>We divide both sides of our equation by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/3/2f3c6262fbacae6ba07fea6f24758dde08078e97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6x$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/4/4f4c2ddde1834f0ea86305aa97ef74b1c623b090.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{6Y}{6X}=\\frac{2X}{6X}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"85\" height=\"39\" />. This can be simplified to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/9/4b9bf74a98d5f001e8849bb7848870d1f09235bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{Y}{X}=\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"60\" height=\"39\" />. So the fraction of the distance to the tree that Miguel runs is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/d/22d6a97906d3b117edc8cfa63fbdde69a0f20366.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{Y}{X}=\\boxed{\\frac{1}{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"71\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p><br />\n~Tgreyelephant\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_7_-_Cheese_.F0.9F.A7.80\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_7_-_Cheese_🧀\">Solution 7 - Cheese 🧀</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 7 - Cheese 🧀\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If you do not know how to use normal math to solve this question, you can also use a ruler and utilize the provided diagram. This gives that the meeting point is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1965f8d70832ded66434c75a7bd52b75090af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> in regard to distance to the tree, which means that the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/8/098ed773743615659f0fb32984f344ba86b60a3d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{ \\textbf{(D) } \\frac{1}{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"62\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/2/36267c5f4ee67ae71ac26988998233a17818f69b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{Note:}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"45\" height=\"12\" /> Even though test proctors, and essentially everybody, says that the diagrams and images in competition math competitions like AMC 8 are not necessarily drawn to scale, they almost always are. This question isn’t an exception. There are some exceptions, though (like the 2022 AMC 8 Problem 24.) So do not rely on this method, unless you have no other choice.\n</p><p>~i_am_not_suk_at_math\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/gzXlOkLl24U\">https://youtu.be/gzXlOkLl24U</a>\n</p><p>~TheSmartGreekMathDude\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_DDM\">Video Solution by DDM</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by DDM\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/nY1hhVbEeBk\">https://youtu.be/nY1hhVbEeBk</a>\n</p><p>~piggydude\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Thinking_Feet\">Video Solution by Thinking Feet</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Thinking Feet\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/BQQcA_IFmQ4\">https://youtu.be/BQQcA_IFmQ4</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_SquishBJ_.28AIME_Qualifier.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\">Video Solution by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3GmtxMC-W1I&amp;t=2239s\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3GmtxMC-W1I&amp;t=2239s</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_in_Chinese_by_SquishBJ_.28AIME_Qualifier.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_in_Chinese_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\">Video Solution in Chinese by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution in Chinese by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV1ScNx6KEP7/\">https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV1ScNx6KEP7/</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8\" title=\"2026 AMC 8\">2026 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2026 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2026 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=2026\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2026 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 18\">Problem 18</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2026 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 20\">Problem 20</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2026 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2026 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2026 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2026 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2026 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2026 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2026 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2026 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2026 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2026 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2026 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2026 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2026 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2026 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2026 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2026 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2026 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2026 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2026 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2026 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2026 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2026 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2026 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2026 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_8_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 8 Problems and Solutions\"> All AJHSME/AMC 8 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017233911\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.055 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.076 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 442/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2272/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 132/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 12614/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.776      1 -total\n 58.35%    7.455      1 Template:AMC8_box\n 39.72%    5.074      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:30762:|